## Demo

* **Live Frontend:** [https://narniafrontend.netlify.app](https://narniafrontend.netlify.app)
* **GitHub Repository:** [https://github.com/Ojhaholic/e-commerce-monorepo](https://github.com/Ojhaholic/e-commerce-monorepo)

---

## Features

* Secure **JWT Authentication** for users and admins
* **Admin Panel** to manage products, users, and orders
* **Responsive Frontend** built with React
* **Backend API** using Node.js and Express, hosted on Render
* **MongoDB Database** for persistent storage
* **Razorpay** integration for seamless payments
* **Cloudinary** for image and media storage
* **Uptime Monitoring** to ensure server stability

---

## Tech Stack

* **Frontend:** React, Vite, CSS
* **Backend:** Node.js, Express
* **Database:** MongoDB
* **Authentication:** JWT
* **Payments:** Razorpay
* **Media Storage:** Cloudinary
* **Deployment:** Netlify (Frontend/Admin), Render (Backend)

---

## Project Structure

```
e-commerce-monorepo/
│
├─ frontend/       # React frontend client
├─ admin/          # React admin panel
└─ backend/        # Node.js + Express backend API
```

---

## Installation & Setup

### 1. Clone Repository

```bash
git clone https://github.com/Ojhaholic/e-commerce-monorepo.git
cd e-commerce-monorepo
```

### 2. Install Dependencies

For each folder:

#### Frontend

```bash
cd frontend
npm install
```

#### Admin

```bash
cd ../admin
npm install
```

#### Backend

```bash
cd ../backend
npm install
```

---

## Environment Variables

Create a `.env` file inside `backend/`:

```env
MONGO_URI=your_mongodb_connection_string
JWT_SECRET=your_jwt_secret
STRIPE_KEY=your_stripe_key
RAZORPAY_KEY=your_razorpay_key
RAZORPAY_SECRET=your_razorpay_secret
CLOUDINARY_CLOUD_NAME=your_cloud_name
CLOUDINARY_API_KEY=your_cloudinary_key
CLOUDINARY_API_SECRET=your_cloudinary_secret
PORT=5000
```

> **Note:** Do not commit `.env` to GitHub.

---

## Deployment

* **Frontend & Admin:** Deployed on **Netlify**
* **Backend:** Deployed on **Render**
* **Uptime Monitoring:** [UptimeRobot](https://uptimerobot.com) to keep backend awake

> Update frontend/admin API URLs with your deployed backend URL in Netlify environment variables.

